{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {Of course, we would like to have
 \{g}{\dn8 n}{ = h}{\dn8 n}{\} uniquely!
 That is, we want the DTFT followed by the
 IDTFT to be the identity operation. To 
show this, use (6.3) to substitute for H1(}{\f1 
w}{) in (6.9) and interchange order of the
 (finite) sum and integral. The argument
 proceeds just as in the case of the DFT
 (}{\ul \b Sec. 3}{). }}
}
